{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And let the young woman to whom I say.</b> He prayed that it be so; he did not rely on divination. So too was the case with Jonathan son of Saul (1 Samuel 14:10). And what the Sages said, \"Every divination that is not like Eliezer servant of Abraham and Jonathan son of Saul is not divination\" (Ḥullin 95b) — the intent is that the one practicing divination speaks as they did; but he speaks this not by way of prayer but by way of divination, such that if it thus happens he will do such-and-such." "<b>And let your camels drink too.</b> For it is fitting for the one who asks to ask less than his need, so as not to impose burden, and it is fitting for the generous one to add and do for the asker enough for his need or more." "<b>Her have You designated.</b> You have trained and guided her in the discipline of intellect, so that she be worthy for Your servant for Isaac."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Resolved נחשׁ throughout as 'divination' rather than 'omen,' since Sforno is discussing the act of divining, not the omen-objects themselves."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:23.434040665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}